From 6a5e29fa1d1f75c3d4dbf6174c6892103c505f2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bedirhan=20Gen=C3=A7aslan?=
 <b2210356065@cs.hacettepe.edu.tr>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 20:01:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 03/71] Rebrand the model surface to GLM 5.3 and add invisible
 turns

Ship the fork against glm-5.3-flash: it is the only listed model, the picker
labels models by display name, and Plan mode gets its own row next to the model
it runs with instead of hiding behind a separate menu.

Invisible mode (/invisible) lets a turn run without ever becoming model input.
CodexHarnessMetadata carries the producing turn's id, so a running invisible
turn still sees the request it is answering while completed ones drop out of
every later prompt. Stamping happens in record_conversation_items and the flag
lands in the rollout, so it survives a resume. Invisible user turns render on a
fainter panel with an "invisible" tag.

Test fixtures keep the upstream models selectable so the picker, migration
prompt, and rate-limit nudge paths still exercise a multi-model catalog.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
